Let me ask you a question. If you were playing poker and got a crappy hand,
you wouldn't consider it to be cheating to stop the game and ask for a redeal
until you got a royal flush, would you? Of course, that is cheating. The
same thing with your tactic to try and get a wand of polymorph and a ring
of regeneration right off the bat. If you want these items and aren't lucky
enough to get them, there are shops located throughout the game where you
can *BUY* them, or you could *EARN* them by killing off a beast that carries
them or something. But to constantly quit and start over like that IS cheating.
Engraving Elbereth as a defense is not cheating; the development team built
that in for that express purpose. But engraving Elbereth, locking yourself
in a room with a sink and generating infinite black puddings is cheating.

As I said before, I don't give a damn if you do this on your own computer where
only you and your friends are in the high score list. But if you are doing it
on your university's computer system where every user is represented IS 
cheating.

Maybe you are the one who should get real!

